    "sn_reviews_kThK6p": {
      "type": "sn-reviews",
      "blocks": {
        "review_amd83c": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"I had a floor-based unit for two years and was constantly nervous about clipping it on a fat shot. Switched to the VTrack overhead setup and that stress is completely gone. The data is actually better too — spin numbers feel more consistent. The Eagle 12 enclosure makes my garage look like a real sim room. Took a weekend to set up but the instructions are solid.\"</em>",
            "name": "<strong>Mark T.</strong> · Verified Buyer · Henderson, NV",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
        "review_gYphWP": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"Spent months convincing my wife to let me convert half the garage. She agreed on the condition it looked clean and not like a \"science experiment.\" The Eagle 12 + overhead VTrack combo genuinely looks finished. No wires everywhere, nothing sitting on the floor near the mat. She's actually used it a few times herself. The 4K image is noticeably sharper than what I had before — courses look real.\"</em>",
            "name": "<em><strong>Brian L. </strong></em><em>· Verified Buyer · Columbus, OH</em>",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
        "review_PQ97FM": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"I'd always used radar-based floor units so I was nervous about switching to an overhead camera system. What sold me was no stickers and no special balls. Just drop a ball and swing — and it works. Shot feedback is fast, the impact video is genuinely useful for finding bad contact, and I haven't had a misread in weeks of regular use. Worth the price for a permanent garage build.\"</em>",
            "name": "<strong>Ryan C.</strong> · Verified Buyer · Scottsdale, AZ",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
        "review_hHCecP": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"I'm not a tech guy. I didn't want to research projectors, figure out throw distances, or guess which mat fits a 12ft enclosure. That's exactly why I bought the bundle. Everything arrived, everything fit, and Elite Sim Golf walked me through the VTrack calibration over the phone. If you want a complete setup without the homework, this is the way to go.\"</em>",
            "name": "<strong>Derek M.</strong> · Verified Buyer · Charlotte, NC",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
        "review_PEhB8f": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"My two boys (15 and 12) use the simulator as much as I do. With my old floor monitor I was always nervous about them standing too close or knocking it over. The VTrack being up on the ceiling completely solved that. They just step in and swing. The lefty/righty thing is huge too — my younger son is left-handed and we don't have to move anything. Best feature nobody talks about.\"</em>",
            "name": "<strong>Jason W.</strong> · Verified Buyer · Denver, CO",
            "class": ""
          }
        },
        "review_qXNc9a": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "review": "<em>\"I had a 1080P setup for a couple years and thought it was fine. Upgraded to this bundle and the difference in the 4K image on GSPro is immediately obvious — text is sharp, greens actually look like greens. The VTrack data is deep enough that I've started doing proper practice sessions instead of just playing rounds. Carry distance, spin, attack angle — it's all there. Solid investment for a serious home setup.\"</em>",
            "name": "<strong>Paul H.</strong> · Verified Buyer · Nashville, TN",
            "class": ""
          }
        }
      },
